## README for Range Query in BST ## 
Benjamin Gofman, Feb 2026

*****

### Instructions ###

The folder contains an implementation of a binary search tree (BST) that stores strings (words).
The BST supports insertions and range queries.

In the directory, you will see the following files:
Makefile, bst.cpp, bst.h, main.cpp

The file bst.h has the declaration for the BST class and the rangeCount function.
The bst.cpp file has the implementation of the BST, including the rangeCount function.

USAGE (in Wordrange folder):
1) Run "make", to get executable "main".
2) Run "./main <INPUT FILE> <OUTPUT FILE>"
   
   Run "make clean" to delete executable and object files. A good practice to do this after changing code.

----------------------------------------------------

### Input/output ###

The following explains the input/output format.

I/O:

The input file should have a series of operations in each line. Each line is of the form:

i <word>: insert <word> into BST (if not already present)
r <word1> <word2>: count and output the number of words in the BST that are between word1 and word2 (inclusive)

All the printing is done in the <OUTPUT FILE> provided as a command line argument. 

Additionally, every command processed is printed to the console. Every printing is also done in the console.

----------------------------------------------------
